<h2>The Solution</h2>

<div class="side-by-side">
  <p class="big">One system, two formats</p>
  <p>
    I coordinated the design and production teams around a single plan, and we
    built the visual system around a central focus area, the safe region for all
    priority content. Every graphic was designed in 16:9 around that shared
    structure, with secondary elements extending past it, so each scene could be
    recomposed for 9:16 with only minor layout adjustments. On the production
    side, the broadcast workflow was automated to generate both formats
    simultaneously, with no second show to manage or keep in sync.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="side-by-side">
  <p class="big">Finding the look</p>
  <p>
    We explored multiple key visual concepts inspired by the game’s vibrant
    cartoon style, testing color, composition and logo design, before landing on
    a bold identity built for the competition.
  </p>
</div>

